<title>USA: Typhoon threatens shipping south of Japan.</title>
<headline>Typhoon threatens shipping south of Japan.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Opal is a major threat to shipping south of Japan in the Philippine Sea, independent forecaster Weather Services Corporation said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Opal has top winds near 105 mph and is near 21.4n/133.6e, moving north at 15 mph.</p>
<p>Top winds are expected to increase to 130 mph, and the storm is expected to make landfall in Shikoku, Japan, in about 48 hours, bringing high winds, a damaging coastal storm surge and flooding rains.</p>
</text>
